Raw widefield fluorescence images supporting:
Wright AL, Weible AP, Estes OB, Wehr M (2025) Ketamine does not rescue plaque load or gap detection in the
5XFAD mouse model of Alzheimer's disease. Front Aging Neurosci 17:1505908. doi:10.3389/fnagi.2025.1505908.
PMCID: PMC11830726.

These images validate the behavioral results (gap detection), which are shared separately.

Hemizygous 5XFAD mice (JAX 006554, B6SJLF1/J hybrid background) received ketamine (10 mg/kg i.p.) or saline,
either as a single injection on P119 (Acute protocol) or daily from P45 to P156 (Chronic protocol); protocol and
treatment for each mouse are given in participants.tsv. Mice were perfused within 24 h of their final behavioral
session; brains were cut in 30 um coronal sections and labeled with anti-Abeta42 (Invitrogen 700254; Alexa Fluor
488 secondary) and DAPI. Images were acquired on a Zeiss Axio Imager A2 with an AxioCam MRm3 camera in ZEN 3.1,
one channel per image. Plaques were quantified in primary auditory cortex (layers 5a-6b) and the caudal pontine
reticular nucleus (PRNc); the imaged region is not recorded per image.

FILE FORMAT. Images are single-channel OME-TIFF holding the 12-bit raw data (uint16) from the original .czi
files. The OME metadata declares 12 significant bits, so Bio-Formats-based viewers (Fiji/ImageJ,
QuPath, napari) open them at 0-4095; in other viewers set the display range to 0-4095. 
Any image converted from ZEN's 8-bit .jpg export instead (because
the .czi was missing or corrupted) is marked SourceFormat / source_format = jpg.

MAGNIFICATION. The microscope's objectives are changed by hand, and the objective recorded by ZEN is not
reliable. Magnification was therefore inferred from image content, and pixel size derived from it:
  acq-12p5x  overview, 1.25x objective (12.5X total with 10x eyepiece), 5.16 um/pixel
  acq-100x   10x objective (100X total), 0.645 um/pixel
  acq-200x   20x objective (200X total), 0.3225 um/pixel
DAPI images were classified from nucleus scale. Abeta42 images take the class of the DAPI image of the same
field (matched by image similarity); Abeta42 focal stacks without a matching DAPI image are 200X, following the
imaging protocol, and single unmatched Abeta42 images take the class of the nearest DAPI image. Each image's 
sidecar gives MagnificationSource and MagnificationConfidence; please confirm the scale visually before making 
quantitative measurements.

MOUSE 1531. ZEN's .jpg/.jpg_metadata.xml export for this mouse was numbered out of step with the .czi files.
Each image was therefore linked to its metadata by exact acquisition timestamp (confirmed by pixel matching);
8 images that were never exported had their stain assigned visually. See ExportRelink in the sidecars.

run-<N> is the original ZEN snapshot number (Snap-N). Acquisition times are listed in sub-<ID>_scans.tsv.
